(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: PM VISHWAKARMA SCHEME \(PM-VISHWAKARMA\) / MOMSME / MOSD&E / DFS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(End-to-end holistic support for traditional artisans and craftspeople) Tj
T*
(across 18 designated trades, including skill training, Rs. 15,000 toolkit) Tj
T*
(incentive, and collateral-free credit at 5% interest.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. An artisan or craftsperson working with hands and tools, engaged in one) Tj
T*
(   of 18 family-based traditional trades.) Tj
T*
(2. Minimum age of 18 years on the date of registration.) Tj
T*
(3. The beneficiary should not have availed loans under similar credit-based) Tj
T*
(   schemes of Central or State Government \(e.g. PMEGP, PM SVANidhi, Mudra\)) Tj
T*
(   in the past 5 years.) Tj
T*
(4. Registration is restricted to one member of the family.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. PM Vishwakarma Certificate & ID card, Rs. 15,000 toolkit incentive) Tj
T*
(   e-voucher, basic & advanced training with Rs. 500/day stipend, and) Tj
T*
(   collateral-free credit support up to Rs. 3 Lakh \(Rs. 1 Lakh tranche-1 and Rs. 2) Tj
T*
(   Lakh tranche-2\) at concessional interest rate of 5%.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 3.0 Lakh per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. Aadhaar Card with mobile linking) Tj
T*
(2. Ration Card / Family details) Tj
T*
(3. Active Bank Account details) Tj
T*
(4. Self-declaration of trade engagement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via Common Services Centers \(CSC\) / PM Vishwakarma Portal) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://pmvishwakarma.gov.in/) Tj
T*
ET
